1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,230
It's the most popular drink worldwide.
它是全球最受欢迎的饮品。

2
00:00:03,230 --> 00:00:10,540
According to the British Coffee Association, approximately two billion cups of coffee are consumed every day.
据英国咖啡协会统计，每天大约有20亿杯咖啡被饮用。

3
00:00:10,540 --> 00:00:17,950
But after the beans have been picked, roasted and brewed, the grounds are often disposed of as waste.
但咖啡豆经过采摘、烘焙和冲泡后，剩下的咖啡渣往往会被当作垃圾丢弃。

4
00:00:17,950 --> 00:00:27,390
With the environment and resource consumption such hot topics at the moment, wouldn't it be great if we could reuse this waste to make something useful?
如今，环境和资源消耗都是热议话题，要是我们能将这些废料重新利用，制成有用的物品，岂不是一件美事？

5
00:00:27,390 --> 00:00:30,490
Well, you can.
答案是肯定的。

6
00:00:30,490 --> 00:00:35,290
The company OCHIS manufactures sunglasses.
奥奇斯公司（OCHIS）主营太阳镜生产。

7
00:00:35,290 --> 00:00:41,270
Max Havrylenko, founder of the company, was searching for an alternative substance to plastic.
该公司创始人马克斯·哈夫雷连科一直致力于寻找塑料的替代材料。

8
00:00:41,270 --> 00:00:47,380
He wanted to 'solve the problem of plastic use and overconsumption', he told the BBC.
他在接受英国广播公司采访时表示，自己希望“解决塑料使用和过度消耗的问题”。

9
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:59,960
OCHIS fuses the grounds with vegetable oils, forming a bond. These are pressed into plates which are durable and flexible. These are then cut into the arms and frames of the glasses.
奥奇斯公司将咖啡渣与植物油融合，使其产生粘合效果，再将混合物压制成耐用且柔韧的板材，随后切割成眼镜的镜腿和镜框。

10
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:04,420
"Don't worry," he says, "They won't dissolve in the rain."
“别担心，”他说，“它们在雨中不会溶解。”

11
00:01:04,420 --> 00:01:13,420
Rosalie McMillan, a London jeweller, uses recycled coffee grounds along with gold and silver to make handcrafted jewellery.
伦敦珠宝商罗莎莉·麦克米兰则利用回收的咖啡渣，搭配黄金和白银，制作手工珠宝。

12
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:21,090
She mixes the coffee with oils and subjects it to heat and pressure to create a compound she calls 'Çurface'.
她将咖啡渣与油类混合，再经过加热加压处理，制成一种名为“瑟菲斯”（Çurface）的复合材料。

13
00:01:21,090 --> 00:01:28,360
Her website claims it has a 'beautiful surface quality and texture' with similar properties to hardwood.
她的官网称，这种材料“表面质感极佳”，性质与硬木相近。

14
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:31,620
What about a coffee cup made from them?
用咖啡渣做咖啡杯怎么样？

15
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:40,490
Kaffeeform is a German-based company that transforms used grounds and renewable plant-based raw materials into a durable composite.
德国公司卡菲福姆（Kaffeeform）就将用过的咖啡渣与可再生植物原料结合，制成耐用的复合材料。

16
00:01:40,490 --> 00:01:47,340
This is shaped into a variety of containers and polished and finished, ready to be sold.
这种材料被塑造成各类容器，经过打磨和精加工后即可上市销售。

17
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:51,350
So, you can drink your coffee from a cup made of coffee.
这样一来，你就能用咖啡制成的杯子喝咖啡了。

18
00:01:51,350 --> 00:01:54,590
And it doesn't stop there.
咖啡渣的用途远不止于此。

19
00:01:54,590 --> 00:01:58,370
Even without a factory, you can make use of coffee grounds.
即便没有工厂设备，你也能利用咖啡渣。

20
00:01:58,370 --> 00:02:05,400
They make excellent fertiliser. You can exfoliate with them, or mix them with water to make a sepia-toned paint.
它们是优质的肥料，你可以用它们去角质，或是加水制成深褐色颜料。

21
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:07,260
And the list goes on.
诸如此类的用途还有很多。

22
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:12,370
So next time you finish your morning cup, save the grounds.
所以下次喝完晨间咖啡，记得把咖啡渣留下来。
